          %title
          .standout
            %p This is a sub-entry of
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
            %p see there for background and context.
            %p
              This entry discusses the algebraic/homotopy theoretic prerequisites for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %p Previous:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology+-+cohomology+theories"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology - cohomology theories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology+-+formal+groups+and+cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology - formal groups and cohomology
          %p Next:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology+-+elliptic+curves"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology - elliptic curves
          %blockquote
            %p
              the following are rough unpolished notes taken more or less verbatim from some seminar talk – needs attention, meaning:
              %strong somebody should go through this and polish
          %h1#section_table_of_contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#the_sheaf_of_elliptic_cohomology_ring_spectra"} The sheaf of elliptic cohomology ring spectra
              %li
                %a{:href => "#the_stable_symmetric_monoidal_category_of_spectra"}
                  The stable symmetric monoidal
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
