              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#the_sheaf_of_elliptic_cohomology_ring_spectra The sheaf of elliptic cohomology ring spectra
          %p
            We will talk about a lifting problem that will lead to the formulation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %p
            %strong Definition
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            is a sequence of pointed
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_n\}
            and base-point preserving maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\sigma_n : E_n \to \Omega E_{n+1}\}
            that are
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          %p
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega E_n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
          %p
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_n\}
            is an
            = succeed "-spectrum," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{-n}(X) := [X, E_n]
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            classes of continuous maps). Then this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theory
          %p
            It should be noted that all our spaces are based and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is a reduced cohomology theory. Define
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(E) := [S^0, E_n]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(E)
            are the coefficients (i.e. the cohomology over the point of the corresponding unreduced theory) of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            %strong> Brown’s representability theory
            \: Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology+theory"} reduced cohomology theory
            on
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
            by an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
          %p
            %strong examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
                with coefficients in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H A
            %li
              %p
                complex
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi BU
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_n = \mathbb{Z} \times BU
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                even and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots = U
                otherwise
          %p
            Le
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1,1}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of all
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi elliptic
                    %mi curves
                    %mi over
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(Spec R, M_{1,1}) = \{elliptic curves over Spec R\}
          %p (we will construct this more rigorously later)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : Spec R \to M_{1,1}
            is a map that is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+morphism"} flat morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            theory called
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{\phi}
          %p
            This assignment is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theories
          %p
            To get a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            from that we want to take global sections, but there is no good way to say what a global section of a cohomology-theoy valued functor would be. One reason is that there is not a good notion to say what a
            %em sheaf
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
          %p
            But if we had an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            valued functor, then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
            would provide all that technology. So that’s what we try to get now.
          %p
            %strong goal
            find lift
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spectra
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mo ?
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi represent
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo :
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi R
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi CohomologyTheories
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Spectra
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{?}\nearrow &amp; \;\;\;\downarrow^{represent}
                  \\\
                  \\{\phi : Spec R \to M_{1,1}\}
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  CohomologyTheories
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            %strong> Hopkins-Miller
            \: use the multiplicative nature of cohomology theories to solve this, i.e. instead look for a more refined lift
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi CommRingSpectra
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi O
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi M
                                    %mi der
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo :
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi R
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; CommRingSpectra
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{O_{M^{der}}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\{\phi : Spec R \to M_{1,1}\}
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            %strong theorem
            There exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi StTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StTop
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectra
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            as a symmetric monoidal category.
          %p
            This and the following is described in more detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          %p
            %strong Definition
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+ring"} A-infinity ring
            is an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi StTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StTop
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            is an ordinray commutative monoid there.
          %p
            So an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            with respect to the funny smash product that makes spectra a symmetric monoidal category, but it is just a monoid up to homotopy with respect to the ordinary product of spaces.
          %p
            For more on this see (for the time being) the literature referenced at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %p
            %strong proposition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+ring"} A-infinity ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-monoidal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
                is a commutative ring
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(A)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
          %p
            %strong Definition
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            with a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \wedge M \to M
            such that the obvious diagrams commute is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            for that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(M)
            is a graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(A)
          %p
            %strong Definition
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            an
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is
            %strong flat module
            if
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(M)
                is flat over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
                in the ordinary sense
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall n : \pi_n(A) \otimes_{\pi_0(A)} \pi_0(M) \to \pi_n(M)
                is an isomorphism of
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(A)
          %p
            %strong definition
            a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            regarded as an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            %strong> Theorem (Goerss-Hopkins-Miller)
            \:
          %p
            A lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi der
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{M_{1,1}, der}
            as indicated in the GOAL above (multiplicative version) does exists and is unique up to homotopy equivalence.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            is the global sections of this:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tmf[\Delta^{-1}] = \Gamma(O_{M_{1,1}, der})
          %p this is not elliptic (its not even nor has period 2), but is a multiplicative spectrum and hence defines a cohomology theory.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            is obtained in the same manner by replacing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1,1}
            by its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+compactification"} Deligne-Mumford compactification
          %h2#the_stable_symmetric_monoidal_category_of_spectra
            The stable symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            recall that we want global sections of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi CohomologyTheories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{Spec R \to M_{1,1}\} \to CohomologyTheories
          %p
            (on the left we have something like the etale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of the moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1,1}
            )
          %p
            but there is no good notion of gluing in CohomologyTheories (lack of colimits) hence no good notion of sheaves with values in cohomology theories.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CohomologyTheories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CohomologyTheories
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of some other category, to be identified, and passage to homotopy categories may destroy existence of useful colimits. The category of CohomologyTheories “is” the stable homotopy category.
          %p A simple example:
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            we have the homotopy pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^1 &amp;\to&amp; D^2
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  D^2 &amp;\to&amp; S^2
                  }
          %p
            but in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            the pushout is instead
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^1 &amp;\to&amp; D^2
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  D^2 &amp;\to&amp; *
                  }
          %p The result is not even homotopy equivalent. In the homotopy category the pushout does not exist.
          %p
            So we want to refine
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CohomologyTheories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CohomologyTheories
            to the cateory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectra
            that they come from by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
          %p
            In fact, we want to lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
            to that of
            = succeed "-spectra." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
          %p The map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi Rings
                  %mo →
                  %mi MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_\infty Rings \to MultiplicativeCohomologyTheories
          %p
            should be that of taking the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (infinity,1)-category
          %p
            %strong Approach A
            (modern but traditional
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          %p
            Then define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            spectra to be ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            objects in this symmetric monoidal model category of spectra.
          %p
            %strong Approach B
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
            \: be serious about working with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            instead of just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            theory) .
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                define
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"}> chapter 1 of HTT
                )
              %p
                in this framework we’ll have a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (infinity,1)-category of spectra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
            %li
              %p
                show that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                show that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (infinity,1)-category
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
                is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            %li
              %p
                define an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
                to be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} commutative monoid in an (infinity,1)-category
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp
          %p
            These two approaches are equivalent is a suitable sense. See
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Algebra"} Noncommutative Algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Commutative+Algebra"} Commutative Algebra
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            categorifies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            categoriefies commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            catgeorifies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %p
            %strong Definition
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            is (for instance modeled by)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                (essentially
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              %p
                (see there for details). In fact, see chapter 1 of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                for lots of details.
          %p
            use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            to go from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            to its corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
          %p
            %strong definition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (infinity,1)-category
            (see there)
          %p
            %strong definition
            morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-categories
            is, when regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            = succeed "s.:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
          %p
            There is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-functors"} (infinity,1)-category of (infinity,1)-functors
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
          %p
            %strong why simplicial sets?
          %p
            because they provide a convenient calculus for doing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+category+theory"} homotopy coherent category theory
          %p
            suppose some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and its homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi h
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to h C
          %p
            A commutative-up-to-homotopy diagram in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi h
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \to h C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi h
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; C
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  I &amp;\to&amp; h C
                  }
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            some diagram category.
          %p
            to get a
            %strong homotopy coherent
            diagram instead take the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(I)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            and then map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(I) \to C
          %p
            The nerve automatically encodes the homotopy coherence. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
            pages 37, 38 (but the general idea is well known from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            theory).
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %p
            Assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            admits
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            in one corner.
          %p
            Then from this we get
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (called suspension objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma X
            in this context).
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi coker
                          %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ker
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to&amp; coker f
                  }
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\array{
                  ker(g) &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \downarrow^g
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  }
          %p
            in particular a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega Y
            is the kernel of the 0-map,while the suspension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma X
            is the cokernel
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; 0
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to&amp; \Sigma X
                  }
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\array{
                  \\Omega Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; 0
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \downarrow^g
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  }
          %p
            One example of this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            %strong definition
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prespectrum+object"} prespectrum object
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with the properties as above is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X : N(\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}) \to C
          %p
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(i,j)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \neq j
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            0.
          .maruku-equation
