            is uniquely characterized by the following two properties:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
                preserves limits and colimits.
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
                is the
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+unit"} monoidal unit
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                wrt
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
          %p
            %strong definition
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            structure on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is given by the following data:
          %ol
            %li
              another
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
